WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Regardless of where a scientist sits
within an institution, navigating

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.620
the modern research landscape requires a
unified, structured understanding of

3
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.580
exactly where the ethical limits lie.

4
00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:13.919
To understand those limits, we have to
look at how

5
00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:15.080
research ethics operates.

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.860
It functions simultaneously across two
distinct domains.

7
00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.540
The inner circle represents the internal
domain, scientific integrity.

8
00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:26.519
This governs the specific methods, aims,

9
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.360
and internal rules of the scientific
process itself.

10
00:00:30.139 --> 00:00:34.040
These rules exist to ensure researchers
pursue true, verifiable knowledge

11
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.040
without introducing bias or fabricating
results.

12
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.040
The outer ring is the external domain,
societal impact.

13
00:00:41.639 --> 00:00:47.419
This area evaluates how the application of new
technology and scientific interventions actually affect

14
00:00:47.419 --> 00:00:48.879
the world outside the laboratory.

15
00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:50.000
It acts as a safeguard, protecting human
participants,
